<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en" class="h-full bg-white"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no"><title>SQL Workbench - Free Online SQL Editor and Workbench | Query local &amp; remote CSV, Parquet and JSON data</title><meta name="description" content="Free browser-based SQL editor powered by DuckDB. Query and visualize CSV, JSON, Parquet and Arrow files locally or from remote URLs. No installation required."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow"><meta name="author" content="TobiLG"><meta name="keywords" content="SQL editor, DuckDB, data visualization, CSV query, Parquet query, JSON query, Arrow query, online SQL, browser SQL, data analysis, free SQL tool"><link rel="canonical" href="https://sql-workbench.com/"><!-- Open Graph Meta Tags --><meta property="og:url" content="https://sql-workbench.com/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="SQL Workbench - Free Online SQL Editor and Workbench | Query local &amp; remote CSV, Parquet and JSON data"><meta property="og:description" content="Free browser-based SQL editor powered by DuckDB. Query and visualize CSV, JSON, Parquet and Arrow files locally or from remote URLs. No installation required."><meta property="og:image" content="https://sql-workbench.com/opengraph-image.png"><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"><meta property="og:image:height" content="630"><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"><meta property="og:image:alt" content="SQL Workbench - Free Online SQL Editor and Workbench | Query local &amp; remote CSV, Parquet and JSON data - SQL Workbench screenshot"><meta property="og:site_name" content="SQL Workbench"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><!-- Twitter Meta Tags --><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta property="twitter:domain" content="sql-workbench.com"><meta property="twitter:url" content="https://sql-workbench.com/"><meta name="twitter:title" content="SQL Workbench - Free Online SQL Editor and Workbench | Query local &amp; remote CSV, Parquet and JSON data"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Free browser-based SQL editor powered by DuckDB. Query and visualize CSV, JSON, Parquet and Arrow files locally or from remote URLs. No installation required."><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://sql-workbench.com/twitter-image.png"><meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="SQL Workbench - Free Online SQL Editor and Workbench | Query local &amp; remote CSV, Parquet and JSON data - SQL Workbench screenshot"><meta name="twitter:site" content="@tobim"><meta name="twitter:creator" content="@tobim"><!-- Favicons --><link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-icon.png"><link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/icon.png"><link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/icon.png"><!-- Analytics (crossorigin needed for COEP) --><script src="https://d2z32053nr86hv.cloudfront.net/go.js" data-domainkey="5szebrpf68d" crossorigin="anonymous" async></script><!-- Structured Data (JSON-LD) --><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","name":"SQL Workbench","url":"https://sql-workbench.com/","description":"An online SQL Workbench based on DuckDB that can query and visualize remote CSV, JSON, Parquet and Arrow data, as well as local files."}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"SQL Workbench","applicationCategory":"DeveloperApplication","operatingSystem":"Web Browser","url":"https://sql-workbench.com/","description":"An online SQL Workbench based on DuckDB that can query and visualize remote CSV, JSON, Parquet and Arrow data, as well as local files.","softwareVersion":"1.0.0","screenshot":"https://sql-workbench.com/opengraph-image.png","offers":{"@type":"Offer","price":"0","priceCurrency":"USD"},"featureList":["Query CSV, JSON, Parquet, and Arrow files","Data visualization with charts and graphs","Query local and remote data sources","Export visualizations and data","Query execution plan visualization","Schema browser","Query history","Text-to-SQL with local AI models","ER diagram generation"]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"SQL Workbench","url":"https://sql-workbench.com/","logo":"https://sql-workbench.com/icon.png","sameAs":["https://twitter.com/tobim"]}</script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/BaseLayout.CrZDwbvz.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/vendor-perspective.CsWI3UxV.css"></head><body><article class="sr-only" aria-hidden="true"><h1>SQL Workbench - Free Online SQL Editor</h1><p>SQL Workbench is a free, browser-based SQL editor powered by DuckDB WebAssembly. Query and visualize your data without any installation or server setup.</p><h2>Key Features</h2><ul><li>Query local CSV, JSON, Parquet, and Arrow files by drag-and-drop</li><li>Query remote data from any URL with CORS support</li><li>Create interactive data visualizations and charts</li><li>Export results to CSV, JSON, or Arrow format</li><li>Visualize query execution plans</li><li>Browse database schemas with the schema browser</li><li>Track query history with replay functionality</li><li>Generate ER diagrams from your tables</li><li>Use local AI models for text-to-SQL generation</li><li>Attach remote DuckDB databases</li></ul><h2>Why SQL Workbench?</h2><p>SQL Workbench runs entirely in your browser using DuckDB WebAssembly. Your data never leaves your machine, ensuring complete privacy. Perfect for data analysts, developers, and anyone who needs to quickly explore and visualize data.</p><h2>Supported Data Formats</h2><ul><li>CSV (Comma-Separated Values)</li><li>JSON (JavaScript Object Notation)</li><li>Parquet (Apache Parquet columnar format)</li><li>Arrow (Apache Arrow format)</li><li>DuckDB databases</li></ul></article><noscript><div class="p-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">SQL Workbench - Free Online SQL Editor</h1><p class="mb-4">SQL Workbench is a free, browser-based SQL editor powered by DuckDB WebAssembly. Query and visualize CSV, JSON, Parquet, and Arrow files directly in your browser.</p><p class="mb-4"><strong>JavaScript is required to use SQL Workbench.</strong> Please enable JavaScript in your browser to access the full application.</p><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Features:</h2><ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4"><li>Query local and remote data files</li><li>Create interactive visualizations</li><li>Export results in multiple formats</li><li>No installation required</li><li>Privacy-first: data stays in your browser</li></ul><p><a href="/docs" class="text-blue-600 underline">View Documentation</a></p></div></noscript><style>astro-island,astro-slot,astro-static-slot{display:contents}</style><script>(function(){let e=async e=>{await(await e())()};(self.Astro||(self.Astro={})).only=e,window.dispatchEvent(new Event(`astro:only`))})();</script><script>(function(){function e(t){"@babel/helpers - typeof";return e=typeof Symbol==`function`&&typeof Symbol.iterator==`symbol`?function(e){return typeof e}:function(e){return e&&typeof Symbol==`function`&&e.constructor===Symbol&&e!==Symbol.prototype?`symbol`:typeof e},e(t)}function t(t,n){if(e(t)!=`object`||!t)return t;var r=t[Symbol.toPrimitive];if(r!==void 0){var i=r.call(t,n||`default`);if(e(i)!=`object`)return i;throw TypeError(`@@toPrimitive must return a primitive value.`)}return(n===`string`?String:Number)(t)}function n(n){var r=t(n,`string`);return e(r)==`symbol`?r:r+``}function r(e,t,r){return(t=n(t))in e?Object.defineProperty(e,t,{value:r,enumerable:!0,configurable:!0,writable:!0}):e[t]=r,e}let i=/* @__PURE__ */ new Set([`__proto__`,`constructor`,`prototype`]);{let e={0:e=>a(e),1:e=>n(e),2:e=>new RegExp(e),3:e=>new Date(e),4:e=>new Map(n(e)),5:e=>new Set(n(e)),6:e=>BigInt(e),7:e=>new URL(e),8:e=>new Uint8Array(e),9:e=>new Uint1